
RAG systems can still produce incorrect answers.

Possible failure modes include:

Irrelevant retrieval
Missing information
Poor document chunking
Incorrect embeddings
Insufficient context
Model hallucination
Ambiguous questions
Conflicting information between documents

For this reason, future versions should incorporate stronger retrieval evaluation, source attribution, citation support, and answer-grounding checks.

